{"summary":"Attempt 1 was blocked before any node command executed. The only established failure was expiration of the managed-cluster lease; there is no evidence that DNS was configured, tested, or misconfigured. Any DNS-specific diagnosis would therefore be speculative.","evidence":[{"source":"Attempt termination and recorded error","finding":"The attempt terminated as `cluster_expired` with the explicit error: “The Antrieb managed cluster lease expired.”"},{"source":"Command audit","finding":"All four inspection requests—two per node—were rejected before execution. No command ID or node output was produced."},{"source":"Executor report","finding":"No DNS configuration, resolution test, restart, or recovery evidence was collected."},{"source":"Redacted stderr","finding":"Harbor repeatedly returned MCP error -32000 for the expired lease, including the retry on each node."}],"likely_causes":[{"cause":"The cluster lease expired before the executor began effective node work.","confidence":"high"},{"cause":"The attempt may have spent too long before its first node command, but the supplied evidence contains no timing history that proves why the lease expired.","confidence":"low"},{"cause":"A resolver, routing, firewall, or Ubuntu configuration defect caused the failure.","confidence":"low"}],"next_attempt_guidance":["Start node inspection and implementation immediately after the fresh cluster is provisioned; record node1 and node2 LAN IPv4 addresses first.","Use a minimal design: install a resolver such as dnsmasq on node1, bind it to node1’s LAN address, and add an exact record mapping `inventory-api.internal` to node2’s LAN IPv4 address. Avoid binding over systemd-resolved’s local stub address.","On node2, configure systemd-resolved persistently with node1 as DNS and `Domains=~internal` so only the internal namespace is routed to node1; then restart systemd-resolved and confirm `/etc/resolv.conf` remains integrated with it.","Verify on node1 that the DNS service is active and listening on UDP and TCP port 53 at the LAN address. Verify from node2 with `resolvectl query inventory-api.internal` and `getent ahostsv4 inventory-api.internal`, confirming the returned address exactly equals node2’s LAN IP.","If resolution fails, collect `ip -4 addr`, `ip route`, `resolvectl status`, `ss -lunpt`, resolver service status and journal output, followed by a targeted packet capture. Do not add firewall or routing rules without evidence that they are needed.","Make the configuration persistent, then perform any required restart/reboot validation early enough to remain within the new lease. Capture boot IDs before and after each reboot, service recovery, listener state, and a final node2 lookup."]}
